body:
This PR makes the TICLGeom geometry one EventSetup product with a simple interface for host code and for Alpaka kernels.

**One product.** `TICLGeomSoA` now has five blocks: `common`, `silicon`, `scint`, `lookup` and `layers`. `TICLGeomESProducer` fills all five. The separate products `TICLGeomLookupHost` and `TICLGeomLayersHost`, their device twins, their ES producers and their HLT cfis are removed. A consumer now needs one ES token instead of three. The `lookup` block has 0 rows for a product without HGCAL cells, so the `ECAL` and `HCAL` products do not carry the 8 MB lookup table.

**Device interface.** The geometry functions are methods of the SoA `ConstView` (`SOA_CONST_VIEW_METHODS` of `GENERATE_SOA_BLOCKS`). All methods are host and device functions:

```cpp
// producer
device::ESGetToken<TICLGeomDevice, CaloGeometryRecord> ticlGeomToken_;
const TICLGeomSoAConstView geom = iSetup.getData(ticlGeomToken_).const_view();
// pass geom to the kernel by value

// kernel
const auto cell = geom.cell(rawDetId);  // one lookup
if (cell.valid()) {
  const auto pos = cell.position();
  const int layer = cell.layerWithOffset();
  if (cell.isSilicon()) {
    const float thickness = cell.thickness();
  }
}
```

- `geom.cell(rawDetId)` finds the row with the lookup block (one table read and a binary search over one wafer or ring) for HGCAL detids, and with a binary search over all cells for other detids. `geom.cellAt(i)` gives the cell at row `i`.
- `ticlgeom::Cell` has short getters: position, eta, phi, pt, zside, layer, type, sensor group, cassette, mask, the silicon getters and the scintillator getters. A getter of an invalid cell, or of a cell of the other type, returns a documented default value.
- The view also has `layerZ`, `noseLayerZ`, `barrelLayerPosition` and the geometry-wide getters (`lastLayerEE`, `numberOfLayers`, ...).
- A `Cell` points to its view and is valid only while that view exists. `cell` and `cellAt` are deleted for a temporary view, so `const_view().cell(id)` does not compile.

**Host interface.** `ticlgeom::Tools::setGeometry` takes the one product. All `Tools` getters keep their names and results. The getters that read a column use `ticlgeom::Cell`, so host and device share one implementation of them; the getters that decode the detid bits (`zside`, `getLayer`, `getWafer`, `getCell`, `isSilicon`, ...) are unchanged. `Tools::geom()` returns the `ConstView`.

**Removed functions.** No code in master uses them: `Tools::commonView`, `siliconView`, `scintView`, `lookupView` and `layersView`, the index helpers `Tools::siliconLocal` and `scintLocal`, and the free functions `ticlgeom::etaFromVertex`, `ticlgeom::pt` and `ticlgeom::isOnlySilicon`.

**Consumers.** About 40 C++ files drop the lookup and layers ES tokens. The offline `TICLGeom_cff` and `hgcalLocalReco_cff` and the `HLT_75e33`, `HLT_75e33_timing` and `HLT_NGTScouting` menus no longer load the removed producers. In `BarrelLayerClusterProducer` and `HGCalLayerClusterProducer`, `std::unique_ptr<...>(new ...)` becomes `std::make_unique`, as code-checks requires.

**Tests.** `RecoTICL/Geometry/test/TICLGeomAnalyzer_cfg.py` is now the unit test `testTICLGeomClosure`. It runs on the default, `ECAL`, `HCAL` and `withBarrel` products.
- `TICLGeomDeviceTest` calls every `ConstView` and `Cell` getter on the device for every cell and every layer row, and compares the results with `ticlgeom::Tools` on the host. It runs on the default, `ECAL` and `withBarrel` products. It also checks the default values for detids that the collection does not hold (also an absent cell inside a filled wafer and inside a filled scintillator ring), for `cellAt` outside the rows and for an out-of-range layer.
- `TICLGeomAnalyzer` checks every column, both lookups and the `Tools` getters against `hgcal::RecHitTools`. A `static_assert` checks that a temporary view cannot give a `Cell`.
